MASTER AESTHETIC & SYSTEM RULES FOR VAULT WORLDWIDE:
Full language: docs/LANGUAGE.md — portable BAD FORM canon (tokens, vetoes, SPECK save format, take/leave). Obey that file.
Overnight agent brief: docs/OVERNIGHT_PROMPT.md.
Product truth: PRODUCT.md. Built visual system, as measured: DESIGN.md.

This is a light field: the category standard played straight, at Linear / Things / Height craft. Not a dashboard, not a canvas OS, not stacked billboards, not a costume.
The lack of costume is the position — chosen deliberately over cassette, paste-up, trim-bin and galley worlds. It buys craft, not blandness: geometry is measured off the approved comp, contrast floors hold, type is sized by ink width, motion explains what moved. A quiet world shows every loose value.
A job is a **card** in the lane that is its status; selecting it opens a **drawer** over the board, so the lanes never reshuffle. Nested work on a job is a **boxed line**, never unix stems. The catalogue below the board is a **plain tree** — stems only, no boxes, no cards, no drawer chrome. The two languages do not share chrome.

PALETTE: near-white ground · white surface · three inks · hairlines · one blue accent (live, selected, found, primary) · one danger red (URGENT, strike).
    10|Ink law: ink-2 is the floor for a **word** (4.5:1). Ink-3 is the tint for a **mark** (3:1) — stems, chevrons, glyph strokes — and never text. One accent; there is no third colour. Not amber, not cobalt, not power red `#E10600`, not orange `#FF5C1A`.
Status tokens are spent in the drawer only. The board stays monochrome so the lane a card sits in is what says its state.

TYPE: one UI sans (Inter-class) on all work. One condensed face on **plaques only** — lane names, job names, drawer section labels. Nothing else shouts. No display faces. Monospace only for box-drawing stems, at the row's line-height so verticals join.

SURFACE: one 8px radius everywhere. Hairlines separate, not shadows. Elevation is declared **once and only in the air** — a dragged copy gets a shadow, nothing at rest does. No gradients, glass, blur, grain, scan, or texture. Icons are drawn inline SVG at one stroke weight — no icon font, no emoji, no Unicode glyphs as icons.

COMPOSITION (desktop field ~1440, one column below 900px; not a PWA, not mobile-first):
1. Top bar: wordmark, one FIND field, filter chips, one primary action. FIND **searches only**. Chips filter session, never source. There is no second input anywhere.
2. Board: five lanes PENDING · R&D · ACTIVE · DONE · DUSTED. Lane head = plaque + count + ghost add. Card = plaque name, hairline, 8px. A card's one quick action is a hover chevron to the next lane; at rest the board is only cards.
3. Drawer at the right edge: status plaque, title, parent, DESCRIPTION, SUBTASKS with ticks. `[+]` adds a boxed line. A done subtask keeps full-strength text — the filled tick is the whole signal.
    20|4. Pull a subtask onto a lane for a `LOOSE` satellite; drop a satellite or boxed line on a parent card to **dock back** (drops `LOOSE`). Physics A: card moves, nested follow, loose stay, leash sags and tightens.
5. Catalogue: stems `│ ├── └──`, drawn disclosure chevron, block behind the live name. First click selects; second click / Enter renames. `_` adds a child. Drag a stem to a lane to set status. Dump tape beside it: txt notes, snap-reorder, drop on a card to hitch.
6. Fold is cued — a sliver of the catalogue stays on screen, paid out of dead ground, never out of a measured region.
7. Motion says **what moved**, nothing else: a card changing lane slides, the cards behind it close up, one thing arrives once, and every duration is zero under `prefers-reduced-motion`.
8. SPECK source is the save format (`speck-os-v2`). Statuses `pending|rnd|active|done|dusted|none`. `LOOSE` marks a pulled satellite. `src/speck/machine.ts` behaviour is settled; a visual pass does not change it.

HARD VETO — product: assignees, avatars, teams, presence, estimates, story points, progress bars, "+ New Deal", KPI rows; a second command input, verb bar, operator slab, dump-parser dock; FIND that creates; a typed codebook to sit down; month-as-OS as home; DateBlocks; CRDT; JSON-as-database; settings app; demo fluff (`BUY MILK`, lorem).
HARD VETO — surface: unix stems on a card; boxes or cards in the catalogue; card-in-card; a second radius; shadows doing a border's job; elevation at rest; gradients/glass/blur/grain/scan/watermarks; a second accent or rainbow status chips; the tint carrying words; text under 4.5:1; icon fonts, emoji, Unicode glyph icons; section billboards, kickers, letterspaced body; Oswald-as-work-type; VT323/Orbitron; green-on-black or amber terminals.
DEAD WORLDS, each shipped once and rejected — do not revive, and do not revive them renamed: paper sheet + organ windows + power-red oval + salt organs (CAL/SEAL/SKULL) + PLACE-drag + GRAIN/SCAN/INV rail; charcoal cassette theatre (housing, jacks, RECORD, transport, VU, CRT wells, Oswald, orange); beige/cream hi-fi faceplate; beige UN seal; NEXUS HUD; paper/black IMP canvas; BLACK LANTERN as maker; sit-down verb codebook.
NOTE THE REVERSAL: the old "SaaS kanban chrome" veto is lifted **for the look and only the look** — lanes, cards, chips and a drawer are the world now. The SaaS *stack* above stays vetoed. Take the composition; refuse the org chart.
